# Campaign UI polish checklist (always)

This web app represents a political candidate. Every edit must keep the UI **clean, consistent, professional, and campaign-appropriate**.

## Before finishing any change

- Keep **spacing consistent** (use the established scale; avoid arbitrary one-offs).
- Keep **typography consistent** (heading/body usage, weights, casing; avoid ad-hoc variants).
- Keep **color usage consistent** with campaign palette (navy/blues for structure, red for primary CTAs, neutrals for everything else). Avoid extra accent colors.
- Ensure **alignment** is crisp (consistent gutters, equal padding, baseline alignment, tidy grids).
- Ensure **copy + punctuation** feels campaign-ready (confident, clear, no typos; consistent capitalization).
- Avoid visual clutter: prefer **simplicity, hierarchy, and restraint** (this is a political campaign site).

## Cross-app consistency check (required)

If you touch shared styles/components or any section styling, scan the relevant pages (home, issues, news) for:
- spacing regressions
- inconsistent font sizes/weights
- inconsistent button/link styles
- contrast/readability issues

## Quality gates after meaningful edits

- Run `pnpm lint`
- Run `pnpm type-check`
